Description: wake the event thread when a reply reader stops reading
 In output_read_reply(), after reading, the reply reader signalled
 reply_cond; the event thread waits on event_cond for reading_message to
 drop, and slept for ever when the reply reader got its reply (Orca asks
 for the voices while a module speaks): nobody read the module any more,
 the module blocked writing audio and speech stopped until a restart.
 Debian's output-stuck patch added this signal on the wrong condition.
 Reproducer: tests/upstream/speechd-reply-race.py (VabaxOS).
Author: VabaxOS <https://github.com/Vabax-dev/VabaxOS>
Forwarded: not yet (docs/sviluppo/segnalazioni.md, report 6)
Last-Update: 2026-09-27
---
--- a/src/server/output.c
+++ b/src/server/output.c
@@ -315,7 +315,8 @@
 			message = output_read_message(output);
 			pthread_mutex_lock(&output->read_mutex);
 			output->reading_message = FALSE;
-			pthread_cond_signal(&output->reply_cond);
+			/* The event thread may be waiting for us to stop reading */
+			pthread_cond_signal(&output->event_cond);
 			if (!message)
 				/* Module broke */
 				break;
